From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rui Figueira <rfigueira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 12:54:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Expose invalidate_inline_contexts for kitesurf font swaps

The emoji full-font upgrade (renderer mode) replaces fontique's
fallback chain after layout has already shaped runs against the
stripped font; without an inline-context invalidation the swap is
invisible to paint. One-line pub wrapper over the crate-private
helper.
---
 src/document.rs | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/document.rs b/src/document.rs
index b15d9ac..60b8a2a 100644
--- a/src/document.rs
+++ b/src/document.rs
@@ -1762,6 +1762,15 @@ impl BaseDocument {
         count
     }

+    /// Re-shape every inline context. Needed after a
+    /// font-collection swap that layout can't observe (e.g. the
+    /// emoji full-font upgrade replaces the fallback chain, but
+    /// shaped runs still reference the old FontData). Wraps the
+    /// crate-private invalidate_inline_contexts.
+    pub fn kitesurf_invalidate_inline_contexts(&mut self) {
+        self.invalidate_inline_contexts();
+    }
+
     /// Cache a loaded image and apply it to all nodes waiting on it
     /// (`<img>` elements, `background-image` layers and `mask-image` layers).
     /// Set a canvas element's framebuffer as its replaced
